course: dictionary
lesson: 6622
title: Saying no with not
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word not is small, but it can flip the meaning of a whole sentence. Usually it means no, or the opposite of what the sentence first seems to say. «It is not cold» means the opposite of cold. When you read, stop at not and ask: what does this sentence say when I take not out?
explain: Not can also say no to just one word, like «not quite», «not me» or «not yet». «Not quite» means nearly, but still wrong. «Not yet» means it has not happened so far, but it may happen later.
explain: Not often joins with a verb as n't: «did not» becomes «didn't», «can not» becomes «can't». The meaning stays the same. Check it by swapping the full word in: if the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Not means no, or the opposite of what the sentence says.
fact: Not can go before one word to say no to just that word: «not quite» means nearly, but still wrong.
fact: «Not … any» means none at all, as in «did not eat any».
fact: «Not only … but also» adds a second, bigger point to what you have already said.
fact: «Sound travels through air, water and solids, but not through empty space.» Here not tells you where sound cannot go.
exercise: «Sound travels through air, water and solids, but not through empty space.» Does sound travel through empty space? | *No, it cannot travel through empty space | Yes, it goes through empty space too | Sometimes, when it is cloudy | Only through water
exercise: «A blurry or faraway photo is not real proof.» What does not mean here? | It is very faraway | *It does not count as proof | It is real proof | It is blurry on purpose
exercise: Ella says, «I did not eat any cake.» How much cake did she eat? | *None at all | Some cake | A big slice | Half of it
test: Inside the Arctic and Antarctic Circles, there is at least one day a year when the Sun does not set. On that day, does the Sun set? | Yes, it sets twice | It only sets in winter | *No, it stays in the sky all day and night | Yes, it sets at night as usual
test: «Some children are adopted: they join a family that did not give birth to them.» Did the family give birth to them? | Yes, every time | *No, they joined the family another way | Yes, when they were older | Yes, but only on Sundays
exam: Which phrase uses not to say no to just one word? | *Not yet, said Mia | Not only tired but hungry | She did not eat any | It is not cold
